                        "glosses": [
                            "In a leaping position; springing forward; salient."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfb420f1-730f-4274-b605-6668f74de7c2",
                                "sense_id": "8cc3040c-8cdb-349e-aeaa-23c97ca2e96a",
                                "text": "Why the devil, can you deny that you've not a partiality for cats, ha! ha! ha! […] the feline species is preserved—the crest is very evident a kitten saltant, ha! heh! heh!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "abb86be5-15ab-490f-a6f5-a39aaf72c7db",
                                "sense_id": "8cc3040c-8cdb-349e-aeaa-23c97ca2e96a",
                                "text": "\"The luce is the fresh fish; the salt fish is an old coat.\" This speech is an heraldric puzzle. It is pretty clear that \"the dozen white luces\" apply to the arms of the Lucy family. […] Since our first edition we have received an ingenious explanation from a correspondent, \"A Lover of Heraldry.\" \"The arms of the Lucies (now quartered by the Duke of Northumberland) are gules, three lucies hauriant, argent. […] 'The salt fis (i.e. the fish or luce saltant) is an old coat.' Without taking it as a strict and formed adjective, I think in Shallow's mouth the salt luces may well mean the saltant lucies.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9535a4d-10a8-4451-8f28-0e37908a7fd1",
                                "sense_id": "8cc3040c-8cdb-349e-aeaa-23c97ca2e96a",
                                "text": "Two lions saltant as vis-a-vis, but reversed, one with head up, the other down."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d113dbdc-4122-4eaa-8ce2-c1b6e94f32d4",
                                "sense_id": "8cc3040c-8cdb-349e-aeaa-23c97ca2e96a",
                                "text": "The issue at the bottom is decorated by two lions saltant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "299e81b8-b129-4f8a-9944-a021754b9fa7",
                                "sense_id": "8cc3040c-8cdb-349e-aeaa-23c97ca2e96a",
                                "text": "Crest a squerrill saltant gules upon a rugged staffe party per fece gold and vert the leaues counterchanged, sett upon a wreath siluer and Sable, the mantletts gules doubled siluer, Botoned gold as it appeareth in ye margent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
